{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>ובה אדע.</b> Rashi explained that it is an expression of supplication etc. And R. Moses raised a difficulty: we say in general that three asked improperly, and it counts Eliezer servant of Abraham among them — but according to Rashi he did not ask improperly."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ובה אדע' is from the unvocalized Hebrew; the lemma may correspond to 'וּבָהּ אֵדַע' in verse 24:14. The reference is to the Talmudic passage (Ta'anit 4a or parallel) listing three who asked inappropriately."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:52.681652486Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}